                <pb facs="0250" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg144"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Diplomatic Agent
                        Jackson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-24">September 24,
                            1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Informs him that the President signed, September 15, a proclamation of a
                    commercial arrangement with Bulgaria, to take effect September 30. States that a
                    formal exchange of notes may be made reciting date if practicable. Reply to his
                    telegram of September 18.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
